+# draft-welcome-call-task: Welcome call task for each new person
+
+- **Jira:** none yet
+- **Gate:** normal
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** <GitHub login> <YYYY-MM-DD>
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** journey. Touches: identity through the existing event `identity.person-registered`; worker registers the subscription
+
+## Context
+
+When a person registers, the advisor must call them. Journey creates a welcome task for each new person, so the call shows in the person's task list.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No Discovery ID in v0.1 states this rule, so the story cites none. A person must give the AC ID or confirm that none applies before the merge.
+
+| Rule (from the request) | Test |
+|---|---|
+| A new person gets a task `welcome-call`, "Welcome call", due on the business date of the registration | `packages/core/src/journey/journey.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+| A repeated event gives one task | `packages/core/src/journey/journey.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** journey: public API `registerJourneySubscriptions(bus, { journey })`, `WELCOME_CALL_KIND`, `JourneySubscriptionDeps`; event row "reacts to `identity.person-registered`"; invariant "at most one `welcome-call` task per person". identity: the event row names `journey` as the reacting module.
+- **Contracts:** none new. Journey subscribes to the existing `identity.person-registered` (`personId`, `brand`).
+- **Schema:** none. The task uses the existing `journey.task` columns.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- The due date is `businessDate(event.occurredAt)`, not the handler's clock: a delayed delivery must not move the date.
+- Idempotency checks for an existing `welcome-call` task of the person: one welcome call per person is the rule, and it needs no new column. The check-then-insert is enough for the in-memory bus, which delivers in order; the persistent repository must enforce it with a unique key on (`person_id`, `kind`) for this kind.
+- The worker passes the journey service to `registerJourneySubscriptions`; the handler writes through the service, not the repository.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Assigning the task to a named advisor, escalation, the step list (A4 task list items).
+- A brand-specific title.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Which Discovery AC, if any, covers this rule?
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
